<div class="publications">
  {%- comment -%}
    jekyll-scholar 7.2 only recognises the switches listed in its own optparse
    (see lib/jekyll/scholar/utilities.rb). An unknown switch such as --sort_by is
    split into a bare "--", which OptionParser reads as "end of options" and
    silently drops everything after it — which is why --group_by never applied.
    Keep this to real switches only. Entry order comes from selected.bib, which
    is already newest-first.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% bibliography --file selected --group_by none --max 5 %}
</div>
